Equating deflection at end B, Let,  [latex] l=3m[/latex] [latex]\begin{aligned}
   \therefore \; \frac{R\left ( l \right )^{3}}{3EI} &= \frac{P\left ( 1.5 \right )^{3}}{3EI}+\frac{P\left ( 1.5 \right )^{2}}{2EI}\times 1.5 \\ \Rightarrow \; \frac{R\left ( 3 \right )^{3}}{3EI} &= \frac{1.125P}{EI}+\frac{1.6875P}{EI} \\  \frac{9R}{EI} &= \frac{1.125P}{EI}+\frac{1.6875P}{EI} \\ \Rightarrow \; R&=\frac{5}{16}P \\  R&=\frac{5}{16}\times 80=25 kN
\end{aligned}[/latex]

